The prohibitions of this chapter shall not apply to noises audible to noises emanating from:
(1) Customary functions and activities on the premises of schools, including athletic events and band practices and performances;
(2) Public safety vehicles, emergency signaling devices, or authorized public safety personnel for the purpose of alerting persons to the existence of an emergency;
(3) Exterior burglar or fire alarms of any building, provided any such burglar or fire alarm shall terminate its operation within five minutes of its activation if the sound is uninterrupted, or ten minutes, if intermittent, but the testing of burglar and fire alarms shall not be allowed between the hours of 10:00 p.m. and 7:00 a.m.;
(4) Automobile alarms, provided any such alarm shall terminate its operation within five minutes of its activation if the sound is uninterrupted, or ten minutes, if the sound is intermittent;
(5) Systems used to warn the community of attack or imminent public danger such as flooding, fire, explosion, tornado, hurricane, or other inclement weather;
(6) Aircraft where federal regulations preempt the local regulation of such specific operations;
(7) Vocalizations of pets and non-domesticated animals, provided any such vocalization shall cease within 15 minutes without interruption unless the vocalizations are given as a warning to or of the presence of an intruder.
(8) Motor vehicles the noise from which is regulated by Georgia statute;
(9) Agricultural animals and activities in the Agricultural Zoning District; and
(10) Activities for which a temporary or periodic variance has been issued pursuant to the provisions of this chapter.
(Ord. No. 24-05, § 2(§ 5), 11-14-2024)

